Description: vaapi_encode: accept libx264 -preset names and swallow x264/x265 opt blobs
 Companion to 0117. Plex Media Server emits `-preset NAME` (libx264 preset
 names like "veryfast") plus encoder-private `-x264opts` / `-x265-params`
 blobs on what it believes is a SW encode. After the scaleplex worker swaps
 the encoder to h264_vaapi/hevc_vaapi the stock VAAPI encoder rejects all
 three ("Option ... not found"). Until now the Go rewriter translated
 `-preset` to `-compression_level` and dropped the opt blobs.
 .
 Adds to the VAAPI encoder common options: `preset` (libx264 name -> iHD
 compression_level/TargetUsage at init, only when compression_level wasn't
 set directly; baked Arc bench map; unknown -> fastest; replaces the retired
 SCALEPLEX_PRESET_MAP env knob), and `x264opts` / `x265-params` (accepted
 and ignored). Pulls in libavutil/avstring.h for av_strcasecmp.
 .
 Effect: PMS's `-preset` / `-x264opts` / `-x265-params` argv reaches a VAAPI
 encoder without error, removing the preset translation and opt-blob drop
 from the rewriter. Depends on 0117 (shared option block).
Origin: scaleplex
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
